<title>GERMANY: Buba's Kuehbacher-Germany can't meet 3.0 pct goal.</title>
<headline>Buba's Kuehbacher-Germany can't meet 3.0 pct goal.</headline>
<dateline>POTSDAM, Germany 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said on Tuesday that Germany would not be able to reduce its budget deficit to 3.0 percent of gross domestic product this year.</p>
<p>Speaking to reporters, Kuehbacher also said the German central bank would resist paying out assets from a revaluation of its assets before spring 1998.</p>
<p>According to the Maastricht Treaty, nations wanting to join European monetary union must have budget deficits no higher than three percent of GDP.</p>
</text>
